<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.16.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01158</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.16.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>5da2b223-bf54-400c-bb85-23f546ff93e1</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section><exercise id="_9e1a192e-92b5-4cc3-8e4d-694ab599ef05" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Here are the first two terms of some different arithmetic sequences. What is the 5th term of each sequence?</para>
        <para>–2, 4 ...
         </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 22; The pattern continues 10, 16, 22.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.16.2 – 4.16.4.</para><para>The correct answer is 22. The pattern continues 10, 16, 22.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="ae3d4215-f4a0-4a51-b7c6-0de5945ab529" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>11, 111 ...
         </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 411</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.16.2 – 4.16.4.</para><para>The correct answer is 411. The pattern continues 211, 311, 411.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_332a2382-f74b-47a1-88cb-4a05bf2c1838" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>5, 7.5 ...
         </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 15</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.16.2 – 4.16.4.</para><para>The correct answer is 15. The pattern continues 10, 12.5, 15.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_4c5df2cc-8470-4d51-a689-97308a1240d2" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>5, –4 ...
         </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! –31</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.16.2 – 4.16.4.</para><para>The correct answer is –31. The pattern continues –13, –22, –31.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_51d5aeab-0fb5-4586-912a-4119fb6a104c" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For each sequence, decide whether it could be arithmetic, geometric, or neither.</para>
        <para>200, 40, 8, . . .</para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! Geometric</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.16.2 – 4.16.4.</para><para>The correct answer is geometric.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_0cb87d46-c2f5-4357-bb6e-b0742f759f5a" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>2, 4, 16, . . .</para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! Neither</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.16.2 – 4.16.4.</para><para>The correct answer is neither.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_4dcc112e-63f1-405f-800b-b4c6cdd6f006" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>10, 20, 30, . . .</para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! Arithmetic</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.16.2 – 4.16.4.</para><para>The correct answer is arithmetic.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_17190c7d-fe9c-4dc9-b7b5-cc966b3c5f44" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>100, 20, 4, . . .</para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! Geometric</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.16.2 – 4.16.4.</para><para>The correct answer is geometric.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="fc75b2e8-89fc-422f-8c59-1e4848f8e18f" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>6, 12, 18, . . .</para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! Arithmetic</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.16.2 – 4.16.4.</para><para>The correct answer is arithmetic.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_214b23a3-97ae-4369-bb95-c6e9c5563ca6" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For each arithmetic sequence with missing terms, find the common difference that might help determine the missing terms. </para>
        <para>–3, –2, ___, ___, 1
            
         </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 1; The missing terms are 1, 0.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.16.2 – 4.16.4.</para><para>The correct answer is 1. The missing terms are 1, 0.

     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="e3e7cb84-d233-4167-83af-7a5523e28658" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>___, 13, 25, ___, ___
         </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 12; The sequence should be 1, 13, 25, 37, 49.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.16.2 – 4.16.4.</para><para>The correct answer is 12. The sequence should be 1, 13, 25, 37, 49.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_9d6f669c-cdda-41e5-93ae-e82b626c39fe" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>1, 0.25, ___, –1.25, ___</para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! –0.75; The sequence is 1, 0.25, –0.5, –1.25, –2.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.16.2 – 4.16.4.</para><para>The correct answer is –0.75. The sequence is 1, 0.25, –0.5, –1.25, –2.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_153b2854-d4fd-4dd2-800c-a12b27f28957" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>92, ___, ___ ,___, 80
         </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! –3; The sequence is 92, 89, 86, 83, 80.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.16.2 – 4.16.4.</para><para>The correct answer is –3. The sequence is 92, 89, 86, 83, 80.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="be845a8f-ef8c-44af-9941-4b30f6d98a92" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Find the common difference for each of the following arithmetic sequences. 
          HINT: It may be helpful to complete the sequence with the missing terms. 
         </para>
        <para>___, 6, 10, ___, 18
         </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 4; The sequence is 2, 6, 10, 14, 18.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.16.2 – 4.16.4.</para><para>The correct answer is 4. The sequence is 2, 6, 10, 14, 18.
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_1b52ae5c-000d-4c4d-9927-e4b1f7fa33d2" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>–1, ___, –11, –16, ___
         </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! –5; The sequence is –1, –6, –11, –16, –21.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.16.2 – 4.16.4.</para><para>The correct answer is –5. The sequence is –1, –6, –11, –16, –21.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_2dbd198f-96c1-41b3-8c00-da290fb2b3f4" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>10, 5, ___, ___, –10
         </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! –5; The sequence is 10, 5, 0, –5, –10.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.16.2 – 4.16.4.</para><para>The correct answer is –5. The sequence is 10, 5, 0, –5, –10.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_3c8b811d-ce4a-4603-86b7-01544732fec3" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>___, ___, 4.5, 6, ___</para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 1.5; The sequence is 1.5, 3, 4.5, 6.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.16.2 – 4.16.4.</para><para>The correct answer is 1.5. The sequence is 1.5, 3, 4.5, 6.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_99db774a-25d2-481f-ba9d-3b0f1f5aa0be" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>___, 12, 6, 0, ___
         </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! –6; The sequence is 18, 12, 6, 0, –6.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.16.2 – 4.16.4.</para><para>The correct answer is –6. The sequence is 18, 12, 6, 0, –6.</para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
